    "predicate": "Ordinary declared Boolean here.active and supported Boolean combinations remain SQL-internal. No numeric/shared-threshold guard solver.",
    "checkpoint": "Entry follows origin/context binding; actor and exact dispatch are validated before binding. Shared thresholds assigned by earlier abilities are rejected rather than claimed to have a general last-definition checkpoint.",
    "helper_boundary": "Opaque helper calls, ordinary loops, writes and cancellation are unsupported effects. Fetch the immediate boundary target without expanding its unknown ability.",
    "data_certificate": "Complete SQL rows validate immediate arity <=1, identity history/cycle flags, order, type/module, guard validity and resource completion before atomic publication; acyclicity is not inferred from edge names or a visited counter.",
    "cache": "Publish ordered typed/native path pairs and real empty markers; a false guard does not invent an empty graph path. Coverage binds invocation token, graph, scope, walker, ability, origin and actor within the query-cache epoch.",
    "native_execution": "Original handlers, queue append order, duplicates, output and early exit execute natively; payload IDs can be deduplicated independently."
  },
